Racial & Educational Justice - Northshore School District
Racial & Educational Justice
Northshore is committed to creating a safe, caring, affirming, and inclusive environment within our school district community so that each and every student, family and staff member feels welcomed, valued, included, and supported. We recognize and advocate for the intersectional diversity in our district, schools, and community in relation to race, ethnicity, creed, religion, color, national origin, honorably discharged veteran or military status, sexual orientation, gender expression, gender identity, homelessness, immigration and citizenship status, the presence of any sensory, mental, or physical disabilities, neurodivergence, and the use of a trained dog guide or service animal by a person with a disability.
Defining Qualities
Overview of Department Work
Racial and educational justice is the institutional, school, classroom, and community work of dismantling systems and structures of oppression and redesigning an education that centers justice-driven, intersectional, community-based knowledges and practices
The Racial and Educational Justice Department work includes, but is not limited to, the following:
Guide and support systems work for racial and educational justice
