PRACTICES
2B:
Students get to experience environments and opportunities that affirm their identities
POLICY
2C:
Students have the access to inform and shape identity-affirming protocols at the school level and policies at the district level
PEDAGOGY
2D:
Students have a deepened understanding about their own intersectional identities and that of their peers
THROUGHLINE THREE: STUDENT AND FAMILY CO-DESIGN
POWER
3A:
