The Northshore School District’s Safety and Security Department recognizes that the dangers of gun violence are significant in both King and Snohomish Counties. The importance of speaking openly about this sometimes-controversial topic and the value of discussing preventative measures is vital to the safety and security of our students, schools, and the broader community.
One of the most effective steps that community members can take to ensure firearms and other weapons do not negatively impact our Northshore students or schools is to take active steps to properly secure weapons when not being legally carried.
Safely and correctly storing firearms is the best way to prevent curious children from accessing firearms and harming themselves or others. The proper storage of firearms also significantly reduces youth and or adults in crisis from using a firearm to attempt or commit suicide, from being stolen, and or misused by others.
Conversations about issues like gun violence with your children and your neighbors can be uncomfortable, but they are necessary and could save a life.
And there are resources to help you start these conversations and normalize these important safety topics.
Normalizing conversations about the correct storage of firearms and what to do in an unsafe situation will encourage students to come forward and share their concerns if they hear, see, or experience something that doesn’t align with what they have been taught.
The safety of our children in and out of school is dependent on all of us. Thank you for helping the district share this important message with your children, family members, and community.
